    "reason": "The changelog line [ev-35cf1ed1a407] and the PR title [ev-33399d918eb5] only say that when Dex is used, Argo CD replaces the `sub` claim with `federated_claims.user_id`. The PR description [ev-33399d918eb5][ev-f413b2bddcd7] is a template checklist that points to issue #17908, which is not shown. It does not say which setups count as \"dex is used\", which values change, or what happens to an exposed environment if nobody acts. The changed files [ev-db80bcfcc7fa] include the RBAC policy, session manager and project-role code, so RBAC subjects or session identity may change, but nothing shown says so. Missing: the issue text, the upgrade-guide section, or a PR description that states who is exposed and the consequence (for example, whether existing RBAC policies or tokens keyed on the old `sub` value stop matching).",
